# Partially live-verified 2026-10-04: BACK on the pattern keyboard cancels
# without touching the alarm's persisted fields (confirmed - Signal still
# showed "Off" both before and after the cancel).
#
# UPDATED with the custom-vibration library: the picker's last row before Help
# is now "+ Custom" (starts the pattern -> name creation wizard), not an inline
# "Custom" row, and the wizard is pushed ON TOP of the picker like the Tune
# picker's "+ Custom tune" -- so BACK from its keyboard lands on the picker
# (not Signal), and one more BACK reaches Signal. The second half of this file
# covers a library vibration: the Signal row shows its name, the picker lands
# on its row, and selecting that row opens the "Custom vibration" screen. Submitting the keyboard's
# pre-filled, already-valid text via SELECT (multitap_keyboard_submit) is
# the same submit mechanism verified end-to-end elsewhere (e.g.
# wizard_create_basic_alarm.seq's label step) - not independently re-
# verified here for a PATTERN-mode keyboard specifically.
#
# NOT live-verified: actually typing a NEW pattern (valid or invalid) via
# TOUCH on the pattern-mode keyboard's note/digit grid. See
# keyboard_label_touch_entry.seq's own header for this device's touch-only
# typing model and the geometry this file's TOUCH coordinates would need -
# pattern mode's key layout differs from the plain label keyboard's (see
# CLAUDE.md's "pattern-entry keyboard" design point: SOUND's note-letter
# grid vs. VIBE's plain digit grid), so its own coordinates need deriving
# separately before this file's TOUCH lines can be trusted.
#
# Keys: TestClearAlarms=10008, TestAlarmIndex=10009, TestAlarmHour=10010,
# TestAlarmMinute=10011, TestAlarmName=10020, TestAlarmVibeCustomPattern=10039
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq
APPMSG --int 10008=1 10009=0 10010=7 10011=0 --string 10020=Wakeup
SLEEP 1

TAP down
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
# Navigate to "+ Custom" (row 6 from Double's default row 1 preselect; rows: Off, Double,
# Double long, Double short, Long, Short, + Custom, Help).
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT vibe_picker_custom_highlighted
TAP select
SLEEP 1
# The keyboard's text cursor blinks until the keyboard has been idle ~5s, then stops:
# wait that out so the screenshot never lands on a different blink phase.
SLEEP 5
SCREENSHOT pattern_keyboard_empty_custom

# BACK cancels the wizard - nothing is created. The picker stays underneath
# (the wizard is pushed on top of it), so BACK lands on the picker.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT vibe_picker_after_cancel

# One more BACK leaves the picker for Signal, still unchanged.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_unchanged_after_cancel --mask-rect 70x25+0+203

# Back out to the main list first - see common/wipe_and_prep.seq's own note on
# reload_ui() not refreshing an already-open sub-window - then seed state
# directly via the test hooks (typing on this device is touch-only).
TAP back
SLEEP 1
TAP back
SLEEP 1

# 1. A legacy INLINE custom pattern (vibe_pattern_kind 1, bytes matching no
# preset): Signal reads "Custom". TestAlarmVibrationEnabled=1 is needed -
# signal_draw_row shows "Off" whenever vibration_enabled is false regardless of
# the underlying pattern, and it's still false from the earlier "Off" row.
# "3 z 1" is valid current ABC syntax and matches no VIBE_PRESETS entry.
APPMSG --int 10009=0 10018=1 10038=1 --string 10039="3 z 1"
SLEEP 1
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_custom_pattern_applied --mask-rect 70x25+0+203

# 2. A LIBRARY vibration: create one and link the alarm to it (the first
# library id on a freshly wiped emulator is 1). Back out to the main list again
# before reopening Signal.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
TAP back
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10048=1 10049=0 --string 10050=Heartbeat "10051=1 z/2 1"
SLEEP 1
APPMSG --int 10009=0 10052=1
SLEEP 1
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_library_vibration --mask-rect 70x25+0+203

# The picker opens ON the library vibration's own row (name + its pattern).
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT vibe_picker_library_row_selected

# Selecting it opens the "Custom vibration" screen (Apply/Pattern/Name/Delete).
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT custom_vibration_screen
